.* MANAGESYS: the Operational Assistant menu for the system, users and devices.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='MANAGESYS'.
:IMPORT NAME=DSPMSG PNLGRP=QHMHCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKSPLF PNLGRP=QHSPCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKSYSSTS PNLGRP=QHWMCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKUSRJOB PNLGRP=QHWMCMD.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS' NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.F1=Help
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION='CMD CALL QCMD'.F9=Command line
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=MANAGESYS HELP=HLPMANAGESYS KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Manage Your System, Users, and Devices
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.To select one of the following, type its number below and press Enter:
:MENUI HELP=WRKSYSSTS OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSSTS'.Display system status
:MENUI HELP='MANAGESYS/OPT2' OPTION=2 ACTION='MENU RUNBCKUP'.Run a backup
:MENUI HELP=DSPMSG OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD DSPMSG MSGQ(QSYSOPR)'.Work with system operator messages
:MENUI HELP=WRKSPLF OPTION=10 ACTION='CMD WRKSPLF'.Work with printer output
:MENUI HELP=WRKUSRJOB OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD WRKUSRJOB'.Work with jobs
:MENUI HELP=WRKUSRJOB OPTION=12 ACTION='CMD WRKUSRJOB USER(*ALL) STATUS(*ACTIVE) JOBTYPE(*INTERACT)'.Work with signed-on users
:MENUI HELP='MANAGESYS/OPT20' OPTION=20 ACTION='MENU DEVICESTS'.Device status tasks
:MENUI HELP='MANAGESYS/OPT60' OPTION=60 ACTION='MENU SETUP'.Customize your system, users, and devices
:EMENU.
:BOTINST.Type a menu option below
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPMANAGESYS.Manage Your System, Users, and Devices - Help
:P.The everyday tasks of the person who runs the system: its status,
backups, the operator's messages, printer output, jobs and devices.
:P.Type an option number and press Enter. F9 opens a command line, F3
leaves the menu and F12 returns to the one before it.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F1=Help
:PD.Shows help for where the cursor is.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F9=Command line
:PD.Shows a command line to run a command from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MANAGESYS/OPT2'.Run a backup
:P.Option 2. Shows menu RUNBCKUP&colon. Run a backup.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MANAGESYS/OPT20'.Device status tasks
:P.Option 20. Shows menu DEVICESTS&colon. Device status tasks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MANAGESYS/OPT60'.Customize your system, users, and devices
:P.Option 60. Shows menu SETUP&colon. Customize your system, users, and
devices.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
